{
  "version": 1,
  "id": "guides/patterns/request-response",
  "snippet": "guides/patterns/request-response.ts",
  "topology": {
    "mainChannel": "main",
    "channels": [
      {
        "name": "main",
        "events": null,
        "proxies": []
      },
      {
        "name": "client",
        "events": ["answer"],
        "proxies": ["sse"]
      }
    ],
    "agents": [
      {
        "name": "assistant",
        "listensTo": ["user-message"],
        "emits": ["answer"],
        "subscribes": ["main"],
        "publishesTo": ["client"]
      }
    ],
    "terminalEvents": ["answer"]
  },
  "events": [
    {
      "i": 0,
      "name": "user-message",
      "channels": ["main"],
      "by": null,
      "cause": null,
      "payload": {
        "text": "Hello"
      },
      "deliveredTo": ["assistant"],
      "line": 32
    },
    {
      "i": 1,
      "name": "answer",
      "channels": ["client"],
      "by": "assistant",
      "cause": 0,
      "payload": {
        "text": "You said: Hello"
      },
      "deliveredTo": [],
      "line": 13
    },
    {
      "i": 2,
      "name": "m4trix:run.completed",
      "channels": ["main", "client"],
      "by": null,
      "cause": 1,
      "payload": {
        "reason": "terminal-event",
        "event": "answer"
      },
      "deliveredTo": [],
      "line": null
    }
  ],
  "end": {
    "name": "m4trix:run.completed"
  },
  "walkthrough": [
    "`user-message` is published on `main` from outside the network; `assistant` picks it up.",
    "`assistant` receives it and emits `answer` on `client`, a channel that only carries `answer`; no agent subscribes to `client`, so `answer` leaves the network through its `sse` proxy and, as a terminal event, ends the run.",
    "The runtime then publishes `m4trix:run.completed` on every channel (`main` and `client`) to close the run."
  ]
}
